    <h2>What we look at</h2>
    <p>A check-up is more than counting teeth. Your dentist looks for early signs of decay, wear from grinding, gum inflammation, and changes in the soft tissue of your mouth and tongue. We also ask how things feel: sensitivity, a sore jaw in the morning, a filling that catches your floss.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Each tooth, and any fillings, crowns or bridges you already have</li>
        <li>Your gums, measured gently in a few places to see how healthy they are</li>
        <li>Your bite, your jaw joints and any signs of clenching or grinding</li>
        <li>The inside of your cheeks, your tongue and the roof of your mouth</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Cleaning, gently</h2>
    <p>Even very good brushers build up some tartar, the hardened plaque a toothbrush cannot shift. Our hygienists remove it with fine hand tools and, where it suits you, a quiet ultrasonic scaler that uses vibration and water. Then a polish, and some tips tailored to your mouth, not a generic flossing lecture.</p>
    <h2>Raise a hand, any time</h2>
    <p>Every room at Brightside has the same rule painted on the wall: raise your hand and we stop. Ask questions as we go, ask for a break, ask for the radio to be turned up. If you are anxious, see our page for <a href="/nervous-patients/">nervous patients</a>.</p>
